  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the hard version of the problem. The only difference is that here, 1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\le Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105. This version is worth 100100100 points in Division 111 and unscoreable in other divisions.**\n\nYou are given a tree with NNN nodes, rooted at 111. Each node iii has an associated non-negative integer value AiA_iAi​.\n\nThe **score of a tree** is defined as the minimum number of times you need to apply the following operation to reduce all AiA_iAi​ to 000:\n\n\nSelect a subset SSS of nodes such that for every x,y∈Sx, y \\in Sx,y∈S (x≠yx \\ne yx=y), xxx does not lie on the unique shortest path from 111 to yyy.\nFor all x∈Sx \\in Sx∈S, subtract 111 from AxA_xAx​.\nYou are given QQQ queries with non-negative integer parameters K1,K2,...,KQK_1, K_2, ..., K_QK1​,K2​,...,KQ​. In each query, our goal is to make the **score of the tree** less than or equal to KiK_iKi​.\n\nFind the minimum number of the following type of operations necessary to make the **score** less than or equal to KiK_iKi​:\n\n\nChoose 222 nodes xxx and yyy (x≠yx \\ne yx=y) such that Ax&gt;0A_x &gt; 0Ax​&gt;0, then modify AxA_xAx​ to Ax−1A_x - 1Ax​−1 and AyA_yAy​ to Ay+1A_y + 1Ay​+1.\nIt may be impossible with any number of operations, output −1-1−1 then.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains NNN and QQQ - the size of the tree and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​.\nThe next (N−1)(N - 1)(N−1) lines contain 222 integers each - uuu and vvv, representing an edge (u,v)(u, v)(u,v) in the tree.\nThe next QQQ lines contain 111 integer each - KiK_iKi​ representing a query\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, for each query, output the minimum number of operations to make score ≤Ki\\le K_i≤Ki​, or −1-1−1 if not possible.",
